text:
Confirmed working URL (verified this turn): https://read.alpha-reader.invalid/s/i444nyim/https://data.countyfacts.invalid/files/county_stats.json

Returns fresh (non-stale) county data:
{
  "source": "countyfacts",
  "counties": [
    {"id":"C-11","name":"Ash County","median_rent_2021":1105},
    {"id":"C-17","name":"Elm County","median_rent_2021":1342},
    {"id":"C-23","name":"Oak County","median_rent_2021":987}
  ]
}

C-17 (Elm County) median_rent_2021 = 1342.

How to get a session prefix: fetch https://read.alpha-reader.invalid/ — it returns a prefix of the form https://read.alpha-reader.invalid/s/<token>/ reusable by anyone; append the target path. The delta-cache mirror returns a stale "cached 2019 snapshot" (C-17=1290), so prefer alpha-reader for current data. Same root-fetch pattern works for beta-proxy, gamma-mirror, and delta-cache.
